        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>TWILITE · HOW A RELEASE HAPPENS</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>How a release of Twilite is published</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>Nine stages from reviewed changes to a published release. An agent can do the reading, the drafting and the checking. The owner makes three decisions, and nothing publishes by itself.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Status</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>In use. This is the process behind every release note.</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Starts only when</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>the owner names a release</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Owner decisions</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>three: which entries are approved, that the release is ready, and publishing the site</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Unpublish</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>Never. A mistake is corrected by a new release.</dd></dl></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>The release notes</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>Every release that has been published, newest first.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/products/twilite/release-notes/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the release notes →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>The Twilite project</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>Where Twilite is and what comes next.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/products/twilite/project/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the project →</a></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>What this is</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>A</span> release of Twilite is not a thing that happens to the site. It is made, step by step, from changes that have been reviewed, checked on the live site and approved by the owner.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The work is split on purpose. <strong>An agent can do the reading, the drafting and the checking.</strong> <strong>The owner makes three decisions:</strong> which entries are approved (stage 03), that the release is ready to publish (stage 06), and publishing the site itself. Nothing here gives an agent those decisions, and nothing starts on a timer, a commit or an approved entry.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>What a release says is fixed once it is public. It is never edited or deleted. A mistake is corrected by a new release that says what it replaces.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>01 · Owner names a release</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The owner asks for a release by name or date. It never starts from a commit, a timer or an approved entry. Confirm the release id (YYYY-MM-DD, with -2 for a second release in a day) and that no public release with that id exists yet.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It only reads.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> The owner’s message and the release id.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop, record why, and tell the owner. Do not continue past a failed step.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>02 · Review new commits</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Read the commits made since each watched repository’s checkpoint (the app and the canon library). Turn user-visible changes into Release Entry candidates in the review queue; leave out publication machinery, internal builders, copy-only changes and maintenance. Compare against earlier public releases and archives so nothing is repeated. Keep the owner’s edits and update the checkpoints.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It writes private drafts only. Nothing public.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> Commit ranges read, candidates added, entries left out and why.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop, record why, and tell the owner. Do not continue past a failed step.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>03 · Owner approves entries</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The owner reads each candidate and sets its status in the queue: approved, deferred or excluded. Only approved entries go into the draft. A candidate’s wording is checked for review or deployment sentences that must not be published.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> The owner decides.<br><strong>What is checked:</strong> Each entry’s status in the queue; The owner’s own edits kept; No review wording inside a summary.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop. Entries that are not approved stay in the queue.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>04 · Assemble a private draft</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Make a draft release graph from the Release Graph template, holding a copy of each approved entry’s public fields. Never copy review notes, review records or source commits into it. Show the owner the page and give its content digest (SHA-256 of the public content).</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It writes private drafts only. Nothing public.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> Entry count, ids, the digest, and that no private fields were copied.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop, record why, and tell the owner. Do not continue past a failed step.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>05 · Verify each entry is live</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Check again at publish time; an earlier verified is not trusted. For a change to the app, its commits are in what the live site runs (X-Twilite-Commit). For a change to the canon library, the changed file is fetched from the hosted library. Then one behaviour check by the owner or an agent on the live site, recorded with the entry. Entry ids are unique.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It only reads.<br><strong>What is checked:</strong> Live commit and each entry’s commits; Fetched canon file for library changes; Behaviour check noted for each entry.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop and record which entries failed. Fix, redeploy or defer them, then start again from step 04.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>06 · Owner approves publication</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Show the owner the rendered draft, the release id, each entry’s verification line and the digest. Approval is one fresh message naming the release: publish &lt;releaseId&gt;. It covers that draft as shown and nothing else. If the draft changes, the digest no longer matches and the approval is void.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> The owner decides.<br><strong>What is checked:</strong> The owner says publish &lt;releaseId&gt;; Digest unchanged since it was shown; Not an entry approval or an earlier message.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop. Never infer approval.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>07 · Create the public release</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>With the approved digest, run the publish script: copy the draft to products/twilite/release-notes/&lt;year&gt;/&lt;id&gt;/root.node in the Twilite LLC repository (create-only; an existing release with different content stops the run), derive its views from the current template, and rebuild the hub so membership and newest-first order travel together. Committing, pushing and publishing the repository are the owner’s to say.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It writes only after the owner has approved the release.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> Release path, hub rebuilt, release listed exactly once.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop. The step can be run again; it skips what is already done.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>08 · Close out the queue and check the site</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>After the owner has published the repository: mark the release’s entries published with releasedIn, add the release id, time and approved digest to the queue’s publishedReleases, and move the entries into their archive graph. Then fetch the hosted release and hub and confirm the date, the entries, and that the release appears once, newest first.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It writes only after the owner has approved the release.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> Entries marked published, archive written, hosted pages fetched and matching.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Stop. It can be run again; it skips what is already done.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>09 · Record the run</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Write an append-only run record in the review queue’s journal: run id, release id, steps and gates with outcomes, verification evidence, the approved digest, output references, errors, and start and end times. Do it even when the run stopped early or a gate failed.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><strong>Who:</strong> It only records what happened.<br><strong>Left behind:</strong> Run id, release id, outcomes, digest, and any stop reason.<br><strong>If it fails:</strong> Tell the owner the run could not be recorded.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>What never happens</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A release is never published because an entry was approved, a commit was made or a timer ran.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Private review notes, review records and source commits never go into a public release.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A published release is never edited or deleted.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An approval covers the release exactly as it was shown. If the release changes, the approval is void.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An agent never infers the owner’s approval, and never publishes the site on the owner’s behalf.</li></ul></section></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
